feat(inventory): overhaul PriceUpdateDialog for touch support and strict margin isolation

**Security & Logic Updates:**
- Replaced ambiguous margin modes with strict "Percentage (%)" and "Fixed (DA)" targeting to prevent calculation overlaps.
- Updated `inventory_manager.py` to strictly isolate margin updates (Percentage applies only to percentage items; Fixed applies only to fixed items).
- Added Gold/Silver category radio buttons to safely filter, hide, and auto-select relevant metals, preventing accidental cross-pricing.

**UI/UX & Touch Optimization:**
- Redesigned the dialog to be fully responsive and touch-friendly (scaled up inputs, checkboxes, and buttons).
- Integrated `QScroller` to enable native touch-swiping in the metal selection scroll area.
- Restricted window height to max 55% of the screen and anchored it to the top (`y=20`) to guarantee ample space for the virtual keyboard.
- Forced the dialog to consistently open on the primary "Gold Price" tab, ignoring previously saved tab states.

**Bug Fixes & Layout Stability:**
- Fixed `AttributeError` crash on launch by updating `QSettings` to save/load the new margin radio buttons instead of the deprecated ones.
- Resolved widget overlapping and text truncation by replacing `QFormLayout` with stable `QVBoxLayout`/`QHBoxLayout` structures.
- Enforced fixed heights (`setFixedHeight(40)`) on input fields to maintain layout integrity on smaller screens.
- Shortened tab titles to prevent visual cutoff.
- Assigned `setObjectName("PriceDialog")` to bridge styling with the external `styles.qss` and removed conflicting hardcoded CSS rules.
